+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Asks for the connected user's conversation list (re-cinq/HALEngine#144). It carries no user id: the list is always the connection's authenticated user's. The frame is answered only when the deployer has set `transport.history: {enabled: true}`.
+
+- A `list_conversations` frame is answered with exactly one `conversation_list` holding the connected user's own conversations, newest activity first, each `createdAt` and `updatedAt` an ISO string, and no `stream_end`; the user is read from the connection, never from the frame, so a frame naming another user's id is still answered with the connected user's list ([validated by: answers list_conversations with exactly one conversation_list of the connected user's own conversations, newest first, as ISO strings, paged as the frame asked, even when the frame names another user](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L111)).
+- `limit` and `before` reach the store as the frame sent them, so a client pages by sending back the last row it saw ([validated by: answers list_conversations with exactly one conversation_list of the connected user's own conversations, newest first, as ISO strings, paged as the frame asked, even when the frame names another user](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L111)).
+- With `transport.history` absent, or against a store that implements no `listFor`, the frame is answered with one `error` of code `UNSUPPORTED` and no list ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED with history absent, with no listFor, or with a collection that cannot list, and SERVER_ERROR with no store detail for a store that fails, keeping the socket open and logging the session id](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L163)).
+- A store that cannot list is answered `UNSUPPORTED`; one that fails is answered `SERVER_ERROR` carrying no store detail, the socket stays open, and the failure is logged with the session id ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED with history absent, with no listFor, or with a collection that cannot list, and SERVER_ERROR with no store detail for a store that fails, keeping the socket open and logging the session id](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L163)).
+- A `list_conversations` is answered off the per-session lock: one sent while a `user_message` streams is answered before that turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers list_conversations while a user_message is still streaming, before that turn's stream_end](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L196)).
+- A client opens a listed conversation by reconnecting with `?sessionId=<id>` (§ 11.3), which resumes it with its replay; there is no in-band switch frame ([validated by: resumes a conversation picked from the list when the client reconnects with its id](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L227)).
+- `limit`, when present, is an integer from 1 to 200, and `before`, when present, is a cursor holding both an `updatedAt` that `Date.parse` accepts and a `sessionId` ([validated by: accepts one with no fields, a whole-number limit of 1 to 200 or a before cursor of a parseable time and a session id, and refuses any other limit or before naming the field](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L253)).
+- Any other `limit` or `before` is answered `INVALID_MESSAGE`, with a message naming the field ([validated by: accepts one with no fields, a whole-number limit of 1 to 200 or a before cursor of a parseable time and a session id, and refuses any other limit or before naming the field](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L253)).
 
